      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "23c2b487a0d8f29700e6ac4089fe525ffc9c872931fc8c2f43167977faff2b4a",
      "rationale": "Expands the named evenOddBody proof term to the exact translated statement syntax; it matches no operational cell and merely names a constructor value.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-23c2b487a0d8f29700e6ac4089fe525ffc9c872931fc8c2f43167977faff2b4a",
      "start_line": 8,
      "text": "  rule evenOddBody\n    => Expr(Str(\"Return the counts of even and odd decimal digits in num.\"))\n       Assign(Name(\"num\"), Call(Name(\"abs\"), Name(\"num\")))\n       Assign(Name(\"even\"), Int(0))\n       Assign(Name(\"odd\"), Int(0))\n       If(Compare(Name(\"num\"), CmpOp(\"==\", Int(0))),\n          Return(TupleExpr(Int(1), Int(0))) .Stmts,\n          .Stmts)\n       While(Compare(Name(\"num\"), CmpOp(\">\", Int(0))),\n         Assign(Name(\"even\"),\n                BinOp(\"-\",\n                  BinOp(\"+\", Name(\"even\"), Int(1)),\n                  BinOp(\"%\", Name(\"num\"), Int(2))))\n         Assign(Name(\"odd\"),\n                BinOp(\"+\", Name(\"odd\"), BinOp(\"%\", Name(\"num\"), Int(2))))\n         Assign(Name(\"num\"), BinOp(\"//\", Name(\"num\"), Int(10)))\n         .Stmts)\n       Return(TupleExpr(Name(\"even\"), Name(\"odd\")))\n       .Stmts"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 29,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "2310190f9336d3807b3f0a9541b7575ee65338e32de301a678715767e85bcc90",
      "rationale": "Defines the named evenOddClosure proof term from the parameter name, evenOddBody, and parent environment; it is a constructor equation rather than an execution shortcut.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-2310190f9336d3807b3f0a9541b7575ee65338e32de301a678715767e85bcc90",
      "start_line": 29,
      "text": "  rule evenOddClosure => closureVal(\"num\", evenOddBody, 0)"
    },
